course: dictionary
lesson: 15826
title: Underarm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Underarm can mean two different things, and the sentence tells you which one. As an adjective or adverb, it describes a way of throwing: «Sam threw the beanbag underarm to Priya.» Here, underarm means the hand is below shoulder level and the arm swings forwards and up.
explain: As a noun, your underarm is your armpit, the hollow under the top of your arm. «Wash your underarms every day.» You wash your armpit, so the word names a part of your body.
explain: Ask yourself: is the word describing how something is done, or naming a body part? Then swap in your meaning. «Throw it underarm» makes sense with "below shoulder level", but not with "armpit".
fact: Underarm means below shoulder level, with the arm swinging forwards and up.
fact: An underarm throw is gentle and accurate, and it is good for short distances.
fact: For far distances, players use an overarm throw instead.
fact: Your underarm is your armpit: the hollow under the top of your arm.
fact: People wash their underarms, and some people use underarm deodorant.
exercise: «Sam threw the beanbag underarm to Priya.» How did Sam throw it? | *With the hand below shoulder level | With his feet | With the hand above his head
exercise: «Wash your underarms every day.» What is an underarm in this sentence? | A bag for PE kit | The top of your arm | *Your armpit
exercise: For a short, gentle pass to a friend, which throw should you use? | Overarm throw | *Underarm throw | Long throw over the fence
test: Mr Lee says, «Bowl underarm to the batter.» How should the ball be thrown? | Hard, from above the head | *Gently, with the hand below shoulder level | Over the fence
test: Which word means the hollow under the top of your arm? | Knuckle | Wrist | *Underarm | Elbow
exam: «Ella's underarm throw went straight into Jay's hands.» What does underarm mean in this sentence? | *Below shoulder level, with the arm swinging forwards and up | Above the head | Armpit
